2. MARC-8 code tables (Library of Congress)
-------------------------------------------

src/include/marc/marc8_tables.hpp is generated from the Library of
Congress "MARC-8 to Unicode XML mapping file" (codetables.xml), published
at https://www.loc.gov/marc/specifications/codetables.xml as part of the
MARC 21 Character Sets specification.  As a work of the United States
federal government, that mapping data is in the public domain.  The
generated header keeps LC's primary <ucs> mapping column (documented
alternative mappings are not used).  No code or data from any third-party
MARC-8 implementation (pymarc, MARC::Charset, MARC4J, yaz, etc.) is
included.


3. Avram schemas
----------------

The files schemas/*.avram.json were written by hand for this project from
the Library of Congress MARC 21 format documentation (Bibliographic,
Authority, Holdings), following the Avram schema language specification
published by the Verbundzentrale des GBV (VZG) at
https://format.gbv.de/schema/avram/specification.  The Avram
specification is available under CC0; the schema files here are original
expression of LC's publicly documented format rules and carry this
project's MIT license.  They are not copies of any schema published by
GBV or others (see audit/SIMILARITY.md for the comparison).


4. Z39.50 client
----------------

src/core/z3950.cpp, src/core/z3950_socket.cpp and the corresponding
headers implement a client subset of ANSI/NISO Z39.50-1995 (Information
Retrieval: Application Service Definition and Protocol Specification),
including a minimal BER (ITU-T X.690) encoder/decoder, written directly
from the standards' ASN.1 module and encoding rules.  No code from YAZ or
any other Z39.50 toolkit is included.

This product includes crosswalks written from the "UNIMARC Manual:
Bibliographic Format" (IFLA), licensed CC BY 4.0 —
https://www.ifla.org/publications/unimarc-formats-and-related-documentation/

This product includes a display macro written from "ISBD: International
Standard Bibliographic Description, Consolidated Edition" (IFLA),
licensed CC BY 4.0.

The national delta layers in xslt/intl/ for UNIMARC-derived formats
(rusmarc-to-marc21.xsl, marc21-to-rusmarc.xsl) build on those UNIMARC
crosswalks by xsl:import and carry the same IFLA CC BY 4.0 attribution.
